How to tag a test (this is checked - an untagged test does not count):
- pytest: put the tag right after `test_`, e.g. `def test_{{ criteria[0].tag if criteria else "F01_1" }}_does_the_thing():`
- Playwright: start the test title with the tag, e.g. `test("{{ criteria[0].tag if criteria else "F01_1" }} does the thing", ...)`
- Backend behaviour (API, validation, data rules) -> pytest under backend/tests/.
- User-visible behaviour (pages, forms, navigation) -> Playwright under frontend/tests/e2e/.
